   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1330db30-6468-41d8-a396-485f10af28c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Spectral Approximation on a Fixed Regular Domain "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "6ae82293-3e38-464a-b966-d410ce84668b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "firedrake:WARNING OMP_NUM_THREADS is not set or is set to a value greater than 1, we suggest setting OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 to improve performance\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from functions import *\n",
    "from firedrake import *\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, HTML\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from matplotlib.collections import LineCollection #need for quad mesh\n",
    "import gmsh #unstructed mesh\n",
    "from firedrake.pyplot import triplot #plotting the mesh\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "opts = {\n",
    "    \"eps_gen_non_hermitian\": None,\n",
    "    \"eps_target\": 0.95,              # off 1.0, which is a genuine eigenvalue\n",
    "    \"eps_target_magnitude\": None,\n",
    "    \"st_type\": \"sinvert\",\n",
    "    \"st_pc_type\": \"lu\",\n",
    "    \"st_pc_factor_mat_solver_type\": \"mumps\",\n",
    "    \"st_mat_mumps_icntl_14\": 500,\n",
    "}      "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f54410b-f068-402f-9ac9-2c61c6fba3a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Mesh Considered\n",
    "\n",
    "In the context of the magnetic advection--diffusion eigenvalue problem, the geometric properties of the underlying mesh play a critical role in the accuracy and stability of the spectral approximation. The presence of the non-symmetric advection term, $-\\nabla \\times (\\boldsymbol{\\beta} \\times \\boldsymbol{B})$, introduces strong directional dependencies. Consequently, assessing the robustness of the finite element discretisations requires a systematic evaluation across various mesh topologies. To rigorously isolate the effects of grid-flow alignment, grid symmetry, and element topology on the computed spectrum, the numerical experiments are conducted across five distinct mesh configurations. \n",
    "\n",
    "Directionally biased structured meshes (with uniformly  left or right oriented diagonals) are employed to investigate the sensitivity of the formulation to the alignment between the velocity field $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ and the element edges. When $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ flows parallel to these diagonals, the discretisation may exhibit artificial stabilisation or anomalous spectral drift. Tabulating the eigenvalues across these biased grids exposes any unphysical dependence on grid-flow alignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "Conversely, a highly symmetric structured mesh (using a crossed diagonal pattern) serves as a best-case baseline. As noted in Boffi's extensive work on finite element eigenvalue problems, highly structured grids can artificially suppress spurious modes and frequently exhibit superconvergence. While useful as a theoretical baseline, such symmetric grids may mask underlying instabilities in the discretisation.\n",
    "\n",
    "To ensure the formulations are genuinely robust, an unstructured Delaunay triangulation is introduced. By breaking all artificial grid symmetries, the unstructured mesh provides a rigorous diagnostic environment, particularly for continuous Galerkin approximations which might otherwise fortuitously avoid spectral pollution on perfectly structured domains. Finally, a quadrilateral mesh is included to evaluate the impact of a fundamentally different element topology and dispersion relation on the lowest-order Nedelec spaces."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "7913d1b2-e3a6-4417-849f-32c3dc25a00a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x1000 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "L = np.pi\n",
    "nx = ny = 8\n",
    "logging.getLogger(\"firedrake\").setLevel(logging.ERROR)\n",
    "\n",
    "gmsh.initialize()\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    gmsh.option.setNumber(\"General.Terminal\", 0)\n",
    "    gmsh.model.add(\"square\")\n",
    "    geo = gmsh.model.geo\n",
    "    lc = L / nx \n",
    "    p = [geo.addPoint(x, y, 0, lc) for x, y in [(0, 0), (L, 0), (L, L), (0, L)]]\n",
    "    lines = [geo.addLine(p[i], p[(i + 1) % 4]) for i in range(4)]\n",
    "    s = geo.addPlaneSurface([geo.addCurveLoop(lines)])\n",
    "    geo.synchronize()\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Firedrake Mapping: 1=Left, 2=Right, 3=Bottom, 4=Top\n",
    "        # Our lines are generated as: Bottom(0), Right(1), Top(2), Left(3)\n",
    "    tag_map = {0: 3, 1: 2, 2: 4, 3: 1} \n",
    "        \n",
    "    for i, line_tag in enumerate(lines):\n",
    "        gmsh.model.addPhysicalGroup(1, [line_tag], tag_map[i])\n",
    "            \n",
    "    gmsh.model.addPhysicalGroup(2, [s], 1)\n",
    "    gmsh.model.mesh.generate(2)\n",
    "    gmsh.write('square.msh')\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    gmsh.finalize()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "meshes = {\n",
    "    \"Left\":          SquareMesh(nx, ny, L, diagonal=\"left\"),\n",
    "    \"Right\":         SquareMesh(nx, ny, L, diagonal=\"right\"),\n",
    "    \"Crossed\":       SquareMesh(nx, ny, L, diagonal=\"crossed\"),\n",
    "    \"Unstructured\":  Mesh(\"square.msh\")\n",
    " #   \"Quadrilateral\": SquareMesh(nx, ny, L, quadrilateral=True),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(10, 10))\n",
    "for ax, (name, m) in zip(axes.flat, meshes.items()):\n",
    "    triplot(m, axes=ax, interior_kw={\"linewidths\": 0.5})\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"{name} ({m.num_cells()} cells)\")\n",
    "    ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
    "# triplot(msh, axes=ax, interior_kw={\"linewidths\": 0.5})\n",
    "# ax.set_title(f\"Unstructured ({msh.num_cells()} cells)\")\n",
    "# ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n",
    "# logging.getLogger(\"firedrake\").setLevel(logging.WARNING)"
   ]
  },
