   "source": [
    "N = 4\n",
    "L = np.pi\n",
    "num_refinements = 3\n",
    "\n",
    "mesh_topologies = [\"left\", \"right\", \"crossed\", \"unstructured\"]\n",
    "tables = {} # Dictionary to store our DataFrames\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Run the sweeps and collect the DataFrames\n",
    "for topo in mesh_topologies:\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if topo == \"unstructured\":\n",
    "        base_mesh = get_unstructured_base_mesh(N, L)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        base_mesh = SquareMesh(N, N, L, quadrilateral=False, diagonal=topo)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    hierarchy = MeshHierarchy(base_mesh, num_refinements)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    eigs, dofs, N_list = run_mesh_sweep(\n",
    "        mesh_hierarchy=hierarchy,\n",
    "        space_builder=FEEC_A_2d1k,\n",
    "        form_builder=A_formulation_2d1k,\n",
    "        bc_builder=bcs_A_2d1k,\n",
    "        wind_func = wind_func_beltrami,\n",
    "        n_evals=10,\n",
    "        solver_opts=opts,\n",
    "        drop_harmonic=False,\n",
    "        degree=1,                                 \n",
    "        eps=Constant(1.0)        \n",
    "    )\n",
    "    # Store the pandas DataFrame\n",
    "    tables[topo] = table_eigenvalues(eigs, N_list, dofs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Render the 2x2 Grid using HTML\n",
    "html_str = f\"\"\"\n",
    "<table style=\"width:100%; border: none;\">\n",
    "  <tr>\n",
    "    <td style=\"vertical-align: top; border: none; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "        <h3>Diagonal: Left</h3>\n",
    "        {tables['left'].to_html()}\n",
    "    </td>\n",
    "    <td style=\"vertical-align: top; border: none; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "        <h3>Diagonal: Right</h3>\n",
    "        {tables['right'].to_html()}\n",
    "    </td>\n",
    "  </tr>\n",
    "  <tr>\n",
    "    <td style=\"vertical-align: top; border: none; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "        <h3>Diagonal: Crossed</h3>\n",
    "        {tables['crossed'].to_html()}\n",
    "    </td>\n",
    "    <td style=\"vertical-align: top; border: none; padding: 10px;\">\n",
    "        <h3>Unstructured</h3>\n",
    "        {tables['unstructured'].to_html()}\n",
    "    </td>\n",
    "  </tr>\n",
    "</table>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "print('A-Formulation, CG Elements')\n",
    "print('Notice the 0 appearing, talk to kaibo/jindong about this')\n",
    "display(HTML(html_str))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b8287d9-fbc5-4319-806a-d48ac20de764",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Corner Singularity\n",
    "\n",
    "We want $\\mathbf{u} \\in L^p(\\Omega)$ for all $1 \\le p < \\infty$ while $\\mathbf{u} \\notin L^\\infty(\\Omega)$, we must use a logarithmic singularity. We place this singularity at the origin $(0,0)$ (the corner of $\\Omega = (0,\\pi)^2$).\n",
    "\n",
    "Using polar coordinates $(r, \\theta)$, we define $\\mathbf{u}: \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ as:\n",
    "\\begin{align*}\n",
    "u_x(x,y) &= \\ln\\sqrt{x^2+y^2} + 1 \\\\\n",
    "u_y(x,y) &= -\\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)\n",
    "\\end{align*}\n",
    "\n",
    "The field is the exact gradient of the harmonic scalar potential $\\phi(x,y) = x \\ln\\sqrt{x^2+y^2} - y \\arctan(y/x)$. Because $\\mathbf{u} = \\nabla \\phi$, it is a gradient field and curl-free.\n",
    "\n",
    "Taking the divergence $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = \\partial_x u_x + \\partial_y u_y$:\n",
    "\\begin{equation*}\n",
    "\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = \\frac{x}{x^2+y^2} - \\frac{x}{x^2+y^2} = 0\n",
    "\\end{equation*}\n",
    "\n",
    "The magnitude is $|\\mathbf{u}| = \\sqrt{(\\ln r + 1)^2 + \\theta^2}$. As $r \\to 0$, $|\\mathbf{u}| \\to \\infty$, so $\\mathbf{u} \\notin L^\\infty(\\Omega)$. \n",
    "\n",
    "However, the singularity grows only logarithmically. Because polynomial area decay always overpowers logarithmic growth near the origin ($\\lim_{r \\to 0} r |\\ln r|^p = 0$), the integral $\\int_\\Omega |\\mathbf{u}|^p \\, dx \\, dy$ converges absolutely. Thus, $\\mathbf{u} \\in L^p(\\Omega)$ for \\textit{every} $1 \\le p < \\infty$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 121,
   "id": "ec9c967c-4081-4910-bbab-008222476bef",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def wind_func_corner_singularity(mesh):\n",
    "    x, y = SpatialCoordinate(mesh)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Define the components exactly as written in the mathematical formulation\n",
    "    u_x = ln(sqrt(x**2 + y**2)) + Constant(1.0)\n",
    "    u_y = -atan(y / x)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return as_vector([u_x, u_y])"
   ]
  },
